R-PX4 R-SO14 R-SO23 R-SO24 R-SO15 R-SO6 R-SO12 R-DL1 R-DL3 R-DL8 R-DL9 R-DL10 R-NI5 R-PD7 R-E1 (slice 072e, Q-D4 of slice 072d): the `roc` proxy with no compiler selected. By R-SO24 this means that nothing is installed (and no rank gives one: no `roc +<id>`, no `ROC_TOOLCHAIN`, no `roc:` pin, no range, no `.roc-version`, no `default-roc`, no `roc` on `PATH`). The pick of R-SO14 is the newest compiler in the channel with a recorded pass for each header hash that has a fact, else the latest in the channel (R-SO23). The proxy runs no probe (R-PX2). It gets the hashes from the header of the target file, which it reads already. It prints no default-compiler line: the stdout of the proxy is the stdout of `roc` (R-PX3). The downloaded compiler becomes `default-roc` (R-SO24). 7 runs, each on its own home (h1 to h7) and project (p1 to p5, the header of `verify/vn1-nocompiler`).
Run 1 (h1, facts): the facts say pass for the 3 header hashes on N1 and N2. The pick is N2, the newest with a pass, and not the latest N4: the hashes come from the target header. `TALON_AUTO_INSTALL=yes`, no person: the answer line, the download, `default-roc` is written, `exec` runs N2.
Run 2 (h2): `roc version` has no target file, so no project: the latest in the channel (N4), with the same steps.
Run 3 (h3): `TALON_AUTO_INSTALL=no`: exit 13 (R-DL10). The list is read first (the pick needs it).
Run 4 (h4, a person, the answer is Enter: the default is Yes for the proxy, R-DL3): one prompt, the download, `default-roc`, `exec`.
Run 5 (h5, `CI=true`, no answer): exit 13 (R-DL8), no prompt, no download.
Run 6 (h6, slice 080, R-SO24 case 3, R-SO6): 2 compilers are installed (N1, N2) and `config.toml` does not exist, so `default-roc` is not set. Rank 6 gives the newest installed one (N2) for this run: one note on stderr (`Compiler.newest_note`), no list of the channel, no download, no write of `config.toml` (a read writes no file, the proxy keeps its cost target), `.last-use` and `exec` of N2.
Run 7 (h7, R-SO24 case 4, R-SO15): `default-roc` names N4, which is not installed (N1 is). The default is selected but missing (R-SO12): the proxy downloads N4 under the consent rules (`TALON_AUTO_INSTALL=yes`), and `config.toml` is not changed (a set default is never changed by an install, so the install writes no file: the lock, one read, the unlock). No repair on a read.
The texts of the refusal and of the prompt are proposals (TW24): the source of the compiler is `no compiler is selected`.
